    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a31d097114dc28c4dc263d9f2327fd1c7fa5931c10e366e3b4018020b216476a",
      "text": "The Sirena Ranger Station lies in the heart of Corcovado National Park, about a 50-minute boat ride from Drake Bay. The boat lands directly on the beach, so sandals are recommended for the wet landing. At the station, change into sturdier footwear before hiking the park trails.\n\nBecause Sirena is so remote, there is a greater chance of spotting rare rainforest wildlife. National Geographic has called this one of “the most biologically intense places on Earth”.\n\nAfter the excursion, return to Rancho Corcovado for the night.\n\nMeals: breakfast, lunch and dinner.",
